Package: MetaboRewire
Type: Package
Title: Permutation-Calibrated Metabolite Co-Variation Rewiring Across Multiple Biological States
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Ovinuchi Ejiohuo", "", email = "ovinuchi.ejiohuo@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: An R implementation and extension of the PhenoRewire framework
    (Della Vedova et al., bioRxiv 2026) for quantifying how metabolite co-variation
    networks are rewired between biological states. In addition to a faithful port of
    PhenoRewire (permutation-based feature selection, state-specific Spearman networks
    with bounded adaptive thresholds, edge-level rewiring classification and node
    triage), MetaboRewire adds (i) exact label-permutation inference for global and
    node-level rewiring under within-state standardisation, (ii) leave-one-out edge
    support, (iii) three-state trajectory analysis (reference -> perturbation ->
    intervention) with a network rescue index, (iv) pathway cross-talk enrichment and
    (v) paired cross-compartment coupling analysis.
